Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0021 + 0023-0037 (touches
spec_decode/depth_policy.py only). VLLM_DSPARK_DEPTH_FUSED=1 (default 0): patch 0010's conf rule and its write into
the requests' depth slots run as one Triton launch (_choose_depth_kernel: clamp, the survival product and the expected
tokens per ms by depth, the first maximum, stored at each request's slot) instead of ~13 small eager launches (clamp,
two scans, cat, divide, argmax, casts, index_copy_), and dead_rows as one launch (3 before). The next round's input
prep runs these eagerly, ~4 us apart on GB10 (Oct 21 prose trace: 109 eager launches between the last Markov step
and the next embedding). Same rule in fp32 with IEEE division; the running product and sum may associate differently
from torch's scans in the last bit, so a near-tie can pick the other depth, and the depth never changes which tokens
come out (rows past it are only not verified).
Test: patches/tests/test_dspark_depth_fused.py (serve image).

